 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Current bounded peer finding: whole-component recoloring is not always taught
+
+Audited generator SHA-256 `561990a5943f15f0be95377574fa0b750ce6db9c3be597295c786bcb9615be1d`, canonical rule hash `108478b11257`. A finite probe of 20 default medium lessons (seeds 0–19; three distinct demonstration pairs followed by two query pairs, contiguous sample indices from zero with duplicate pairs skipped) found a visible-demo-fit/query-disagreement witness. At seed 2, demonstration indices 0–2 have profiles `mixed_component_sizes`, `bidirectional_x`, and `edge_positive`. The plausible wrong rule “recolor only the cells belonging to straight diagonal runs of at least three” fits all three demonstrations. Query index 4 (`branched_positive`) requires recoloring the entire connected component and disagrees with that rival. The other query, index 3 (`dense_negative_component`), agrees.
+
+All five seed-2 labels were executed with the canonical rule through protected Racket and matched the diagnostic Python labels. The retained receipt binds the runtime binary, prelude, rule, generator, inputs, outputs, and rival predictions. The Python screening found teaching holes for diagonal-cells-only in 5/20 lessons, down-right-only in 3/20, and threshold-two in 1/20; only the first diagonal-cells-only witness was replayed in Racket. Two duplicate pairs were skipped and no generation errors occurred. These finite counts do not establish a full distribution rate or broad qualification. Generator and approval state remain unchanged; the finding is open for a future lesson-construction repair.
+
+Reproducer: `generators/59a7762bc6da/workspace/peer_probe.py`. Evidence: `checks/59a7762bc6da/peer_probe.json` and `checks/59a7762bc6da/peer-command-v2.json`. Run from the outer packet directory: `WORK/.venv/bin/python review.py run --receipt checks/59a7762bc6da/peer-command-v2.json python generators/59a7762bc6da/workspace/peer_probe.py`.
