+## Current bounded peer finding
+
+Source `8e8e70106fdf4ba68442985b4b19cbb06137775a323cab0f644969b61c5c5ca1`
+still has a teaching/domain gap. A focused check executed 17 protected Racket
+reference evaluations with rule `dfecf6d0b7a6`: 12 ordinary medium draws at seed
+`20261024`, two explicit texture draws, and all three canonical labeled pairs.
+The ordinary draws all fit three wrong rules: translate each entire row right,
+circularly translate each row right, and move cells sequentially right to left.
+Using ordinary draws 0, 1 and 2 as demonstrations and the generated
+`cell_at_right_edge` texture as query yields a validator-accepted constructed
+lesson where both row-translation rivals fit every demonstration and disagree
+with the Racket query label. This deliberately combines generator calls with
+different overrides; it is not a default emitted episode.
+
+The `cells_blocked` texture and all three canonical inputs fail `self_check`,
+despite canonical labels agreeing with executed Racket. The blocked texture
+separates the sequential rival, but is not an accepted-query witness. This
+confirms the ordinary domain omits the task's blocked-cell distinction. These
+findings do not resolve or upgrade the two existing unresolved audits.
+
+Evidence and executable reproduction: `checks/85305305afdf/probe.py`,
+`checks/85305305afdf/probe.json`, and
+`checks/85305305afdf/probe-command.json` in the review return. Run from the outer
+workspace: `WORK/.venv/bin/python review.py run python ../checks/85305305afdf/probe.py`.
+Rivals were executed in Python; labels were executed in protected Racket. No
+full battery, parameter sweep, source repair, or approval was performed.
